/**
 * @page topic_server Server Application
 * @ingroup module_server
 * @brief Multi-client server architecture and ownership model.
 *
 * The server combines a shared network runtime with per-peer media state. The
 * network layer accepts and drives connections; server callbacks authenticate
 * peers and connect them to the media mixer, renderer, statistics, and TUI.
 *
 * @section server_layers Layers
 *
 * - `network_server_t` owns listeners, backend workers, and connection registry.
 * - `network_connection_t` owns one peer transport, callbacks, handshake, and
 *   lifecycle state.
 * - `client_info_t` owns peer-specific terminal/media state and render workers.
 * - ACIP handlers validate and dispatch packets above the transport boundary.
 * - Stream/mixer/render modules produce personalized video and audio output.
 *
 * @section server_flow Peer flow
 *
 * A listener creates a connection, the server callback installs application
 * context, and ACIP negotiation authenticates the peer. Once ready, the server
 * sends state, accepts media into bounded buffers/mixers, and produces output
 * through type-specific ACIP send helpers.
 *
 * @section server_concurrency Concurrency
 *
 * Network callbacks are serialized per connection and run outside backend event
 * loops. Media render workers may run per client. Shared registries and mixers
 * use their synchronization APIs; callbacks must not hold locks while joining
 * workers or performing blocking I/O.
 *
 * @section server_shutdown Shutdown
 *
 * Stop accepting work, request network shutdown, stop and join media producers,
 * drain connection callbacks, remove mixer sources, and release application
 * state. The transport remains owned by the network connection until close
 * callbacks complete.
 *
 * @see topic_server_main
 * @see topic_server_client
 * @see topic_network
 */
